From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alesx2io <96351978+alesx2io@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:23:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dash: use the AOSP lmkd defaults

kill_timeout_ms 50, stall_limit_critical 40 and filecache_min_kb 150 MB come
from the HyperOS vendor properties, where they work together with the
Xiaomi memory management that keeps apps alive by other means. On AOSP they
made lmkd kill background apps earlier than needed on a 12 GB device.

Use the AOSP defaults (100 ms, 100, 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vendor.prop | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vendor.prop b/vendor.prop
index 6cdd022..ba676db 100644
--- a/vendor.prop
+++ b/vendor.prop
@@ -251,11 +251,6 @@ debug.hwui.target_cpu_time_percent=30
 debug.hwui.use_hint_manager=true
 debug.sf.enable_adpf_cpu_hint=true
 
-# LMK tuning
-ro.lmk.filecache_min_kb=153600
-ro.lmk.kill_timeout_ms=50
-ro.lmk.stall_limit_critical=40
-
 # Media
 debug.stagefright.c2inputsurface=-1
 media.c2.dmabuf.padding=3072
